values ('f2a3b4c5-6d7e-4f79-8a89-9c0d1e2f3a99', 'foundations-of-education', 'Foundations of Education', 'This course introduces education as a historical, philosophical, sociological, political, legal, ethical, and professional field. Students examine the purposes of schooling, U.S. education history, learning and development, curriculum and assessment, governance and finance, law and policy, equity and opportunity, teacher professionalism, comparative education, and current reform debates. The course prepares future educators to connect classroom practice with the broader systems and values that shape schooling.');

