al theory"}], "description": "Students compare learning theories as lenses for instructional decisions."}, {"id": "7fa331fb-dac8-4d80-85aa-5b7fe3d0609c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Development, motivation, and identity", "children": [{"id": "f5cdc4b1-a060-40df-b906-e56685755bf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Child and adolescent development"}, {"id": "2c6a3cad-10a4-4361-b2bb-94dc20577570", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-regulation and metacognition"}, {"id": "6d5b8550-4c7e-4ace-bda7-88ee19a5888e", "type": "concept", "title": "Motivation, identity, and learner agency"}], "description": "Students learn that learning is shaped by development, motivation, belonging, and agency."}, {"id": "1ff71254-3e3d-4fe1-a025-78855d3bf977", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence standards and learner variability", "children": [{"id": "9df3c00c-23de-420c-92d9-426631ced3a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Memory, retrieval practice, spacing, and feedback"}, {"id": "b1c5ad15-c980-4b8b-bdf3-d8612bf978d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Neuroscience myths and evidence quality"}, {"id": "94f68722-d308-4fe1-8108-ad881d664bf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal Design for Learning and inclusion"}], "description": "Students learn to evaluate learning-science claims carefully and design for diverse learners."}]}, {"id": "33e20cd8-e646-49a9-87ac-4fd4ddb9b284", "type": "topic", "title": "Curriculum, Standards, and Assessment Foundations", "description": "Curriculum and assessment translate educational aims into daily work. This unit shows how standards, learning goals, tasks, evidence, and feedback connect.", "children": [{"id": "5f85499e-36f1-4e4c-bf1e-0ef3acd3b280", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Curriculum theory and design", "children": [{"id": "38754dc4-838f-46f5-b9fd-c93e69cd3cbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Curriculum models and design traditions"}, {"id": "c79df26d-cfe9-4315-b72e-f57a0a8659ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards, competencies, and learning progressions"}, {"i